# Temple of Cultivation: "{2}{G}, {T}: Transform this land. Activate only if you control ten or more permanents and only as a sorcery." Ojer Kaslem was killed on turn 2
# and came back as the Temple (Bot1 had cast Mox Emerald, Mox Pearl, Mox Jet and Mox Ruby on turn 1, and casts a Mox Sapphire on turn 3). On turn 7 Bot1 has the Temple, the
# Forest and five Moxen: seven permanents. Secure the Wastes for two makes two Warriors, nine permanents, and the Temple is refused with the mana to pay for it (the
# Emerald, the Sapphire and the Forest). Casting the Memnite makes ten; the Temple is refused at the beginning of combat (only as a sorcery, CR 602.5d) and in the second
# main phase it transforms back into Ojer Kaslem, tapped for the cost (CR 712.18: the same permanent).

